# OpticWise SB7 BrandScript Rule

Whenever you are asked to write, edit, reposition, draft, or proof anything that represents **OpticWise (OW)** — externally or internally — you MUST follow the OW SB7 BrandScript canon.

This applies to: web copy (this `opticwise-html` site and any related property), blog posts, LinkedIn posts/articles, sales decks, talk tracks, objection handling, outbound emails, partner communications, board materials, podcast intros, ad copy, press materials, internal memos, and any other output that carries the OW name.

**Read the connected canon before writing a single word:**

@OW_SB7_brandscript.md

The connected file is the synthesized brandscript canon — SB7 narrative, voice, trademarks, banned words, PPP 5C™ plan, two-layer model, asset-manager mindset overlay, approved Wins & Nightmares, Big Three Plays diagnostic, NOI benchmarks, market-context thesis, sales reframes, competitive posture, and pre-publish checklist. It is non-negotiable and overrides anything in this codebase that contradicts it.

**Acronyms (define on request, never substitute):**
- **OW** = OpticWise
- **PPP** = Peak Property Performance®

