If a content question lands outside the connected canon, ask before improvising. Never invent client names, numbers, quotes, case studies, or proof points.

## Hard rules (do not violate, ever)

- Always say **"data & digital infrastructure"** — never "infrastructure" alone.
- OpticWise is **NOT "PropTech."** Ever.
- Use **"owner"** (not "REIT"), **"review"** (not "audit" for the OW engagement — PPP Audit™ stays as a trademark), and **"operations" / "utilities optimization"** (never "ESG").
- Every trademark, every mention: **Peak Property Performance®, PPP 5C™, BoT®, Building of Things®, ElasticISP®, 5S®, Property Brain™, Portfolio Brain™.**
- Default audience lens is the **asset manager**. PMs, IT, and engineers are read-through stakeholders, not the buyer.
- Never invent client names, metrics, quotes, case studies, or outcomes. Use only the approved Wins & Nightmares (WIN-001/002/003 and NM-001 through NM-006). Otherwise frame as *"a common pattern we see…"* with **no numbers**.
- Use the reframing line at least once per long-form piece: **"If you don't own your data & digital infrastructure, your vendors do."**
- Default closer when the close calls for it: **"Own your data & digital infrastructure. Operate with strategic foresight. Build for the long game."**

